# TOUCH CONTROLS card check (not a store asset): the in-game help card
# reached from the touch pause screen's CONTROLS band, with its INPUT
# METHOD / HANDEDNESS option bands under the gesture table. Render with
# NEWTONIA_FORCE_TOUCH=1 (shots/run.sh shots/touchhelp.shot). The first
# tap dismisses the first-game auto-shown card (one_hand), `key p`
# pauses, and the last tap lands on the pause screen's CONTROLS band
# (hung under the "Paused" title with a gap and pad that scale with the
# portrait stretch; its zone starts at the subtitle's descent: 0.55..0.65
# of the height in landscape, ~0.52..0.60 in portrait, so 0.58 hits it
# in both). Add a tap
# anywhere in 0.69..0.84 of the height in landscape (portrait scales the
# block 1.6x and anchors it lower — 720x1560: 0.57..0.65; the bands are
# finger-tall on purpose — left half INPUT METHOD, right half
# HANDEDNESS) to see the bands cycle and the table swap.
game 1
sim 1500
camera fixed
ship 0 0 0
asteroid 700 400 tough
asteroid -800 300 armoured
asteroid 300 -800
one_hand centre
tap 0.5 0.5 200
key p 500
tap 0.5 0.58 900
